# A50.1 independent read-only stop-capability observer

## A50.6 bounded original-connection reconciliation

The separately reviewed observation-surface proposal2 and interface1 add an
initial-only public notification channel. Original A/B/C/D failures remain
UNKNOWN. This implementation does not retry them or confer task50 acceptance.

Use `--probe static-preflight` with `StaticRuntimeProbeAdmission`, then
`--probe stop-capability` with a `RuntimeProbeAdmission` containing
`static_preflight`, `operator`, `notification_schemas`, `fixture_plan`,
`handoff_path`, `recorder_exit_path`, explicit `auditor.retention`, and
`live_clock`, plus shared `source_profile`. The latter is
PythonBootstrapSourceProfile: exact interpreter, stdlib_root, two actual reviewed
readonly profile-helper commands (`-B` and `-I -B`), and rederived bootstrap rows
`{name,path:resolved regular file,sha256,observed_path:literal module.__file__}`.
Both raw samples must agree. Startup sitecustomize's installed logical symlink is
allowed only by its exact name, observed alias, resolved file and hash; there is
no site-directory or arbitrary symlink allowance. Static/live/final module
closures rehash every actual loaded file and pin each auditor import to its raw
source entry. Unlisted site/PYTHONPATH imports and source/body changes refuse.
New actual executable argv uses pinned Python `-B` and the exact
materialized entrypoint. Legacy invocation without static_preflight retains its
original strict witness path.

The static actor performs full cold/tree/review/source/schema/runtime/layout
checks without application RPCs. It emits `static-report.json` with exact raw
`auditor_context`/`operator_context`, both retention refs, literal `host_argv`
and `exec_argv`, and actual actor scope/clock. Future thread/turn/PIDs are absent.
Fixture output and observer run remain absent; their owned literal parents exist.
The channel directory exists fresh and empty, with owned UID/dev/inode.

The live actor reopens that actual completed static command, all authority and
pack hashes, both full current source manifests and executing import/module
paths, tools/runtime/schema pins, and prospective clean linked Git identities.
It emits `observer-ready.json` only after these checks. Its source field is the
exact auditor pin object, fresh_manifest contains two raw equality receipts,
and actual argv/process/scope are independently observed. The original host
clock predates Popen, not readiness: `PreflightHostCommandIntent` binds literal
enclosing systemd-run actor argv/cwd and start; `ActorExec` binds the actual
authorization, same surviving PID/birth, actual scope and executed probe argv.
`live_clock.actor_exec_path` is a promised literal path, not a circular hash.
Neither stage may exceed120000ms; no clock reset is permitted.

The exact fsynced FixtureBound handoff binds that Ready, separately reviewed
operator, actual fresh creation/goal/invocation/payload receipts and original
channel. Missing/stale/mismatched provenance is UNKNOWN. Channel JSON uses strict
duplicate/nonfinite rejection and literal schema1. All frames/events/checkpoints
reopen absolute regular exact-byte refs. The reader rederives contiguous frame
and event indexes, previous refs, five category counters, allowed reply IDs,
method counts, actual drained buffer/peer/source and monotonic coverage. Unknown
owned tools/private bodies, missing/corrupt records, stale/gapped/undrained
coverage, errors,128 frames,64 ordinary checkpoints or combined32MiB violations
refuse. Checkpoint names are checkpoint-0001.json onward; channel-final.json
explicitly links the separate final checkpoint, at most65. Channel output is
outside every original writer/source/commonGit/native/observer scope; there are
no recorder PID or write-FD exemptions.

The dedicated initial join preserves empty native item history as empty. Actual
turn/started plus one inProgress command item/started on the original connection
must match exact fresh identities, observed cwd/userShell and independently
rendered command digest, with no earlier completion. Complete six native reads
must show the active exact turn and absent goal. Independent read/kernel interval
must be at most5s, with actual payload argv/incarnation/scope/native ancestry,
known births, native-handle correspondence and complete writer coverage. The
fresh drained prefix must cover its end. Event and kernel are jointly required;
neither substitutes for the other or enters the native item list.

While the turn is active, later complete reads/kernel samples may still have
empty item history; they are retained without stopped acceptance. Terminal
observations always require original strict native_facts: same command now in
complete actual item history, integer exit, idle exact thread/terminal turn,
absent goal, empty queue/handles, every known birth gone, empty/disappeared owned
scope and no unknown writer/scan gap. Actual concordant completion events and
continuous drained prefixes supplement both samples, separated by at least5s.

After both samples are durable, `channel-close-request.json` controls only the
recorder's passive connection. Final seal requires a full error-free drained
ChannelFinal plus RecorderHostExit: reopened actual enclosing command argv,
exit/stdout/stderr/clock, ActorExec/source/birth, actual reap/post-process read
and independently empty/disappeared recorder scope. Unknown/missing final/exit
or any live old birth refuses. Full original cold/tree/runtime/tool checks repeat
before publication inside the unchanged clock. No native stop, cleanup, claim
release, model dispatch or Kata mutation is implemented.

This is a partial task50 preflight seam, not task50 acceptance. It observes one
separately admitted, explicitly authorized cooperative host fixture. It cannot
create a thread/turn/goal, queue work, interrupt tools, stop processes, release a
claim, clean a workspace, repair source or modify Kata. The `thread/shellCommand`
fixture is unsandboxed by native contract; its success does not establish model
worker sandbox, common-Git or nested-Insula grants. Those proofs, isolated Kata,
and shared writer/resource reconciliation remain prerequisites to managed work.

## Invocation and authority

Invoke the immutable materialized helper from the owned output parent:

```
python3 /ABS/admitted-A50/tests/collab/audit_support/runtime_probe.py \
  --probe stop-capability --authorization /ABS/admission.json --output /ABS/new-run
```

The enclosing admitted host command must enforce the same wall-time bound and
retain its actual argv, cwd, exit, stdout/stderr and resource receipt. The helper
also arms its own wall deadline. Its only runtime mutations are protocol
`initialize`/`initialized` and WebSocket Pong; application methods are restricted
before send to six exact-thread reads. No managed launch permission follows.

Every artifact reference is `{path: absolute regular nonsymlink file,
sha256: literal SHA256}`; changed/missing bytes refuse. JSON protocol objects have
integer `schema_version:1`, no duplicate keys or nonfinite numbers. Original
source/review/proof artifacts are never rewritten.

`RuntimeProbeAdmission` has these required fields:

- `kind:"RuntimeProbeAdmission"`, `probe:"stop-capability"`.
- `authors:{producer,auditor,reviewer}`: three distinct canonical identities.
- `auditor:{candidate,source,materialization,review}`: exact single-parent commit,
  source path and references. `coverage` pins the unchanged committed oracle
  coverage. A formal `independent-auditor-source-review` must bind its candidate,
  parent, tree, source, materialization, retention, author and reviewer; verdict
  alone is insufficient. Fresh cold-pack reconstruction and complete filesystem
  tree equality are independently repeated before opening the socket and source
  union checks repeated before report publication.
- `user_authority`: retained explicit admission record for this bounded probe.
- `runtime:{transport:"websocket-over-owned-unix",endpoint:{path,uid,device,inode},
  daemon:{boot_id,pid,start_ticks,executable},schemas,schema_provenance}`.
  Actual socket type/incarnation, UID/SO_PEERCRED, daemon birth and `/proc/PID/exe`
  are checked. Shared daemon identity never establishes worker ownership.
- `resources:{observer_scope:{path,device,inode},deadline_ms,request_timeout_ms,
  max_pages,max_items,max_output_bytes,output_root}`. Bounds are respectively
  <=120000ms, <=2000ms, <=16 pages per list, <=512 total entries per snapshot,
  <=33554432 retained bytes. The observer scope is exclusive to its own PID,
  <=256MiB RAM, zero swap, zero observed OOM kills, named
  `sureal-sustained-collab-*.scope`. The output parent/cwd is an owned absolute
  nonsymlink directory; output is fresh and separate from fixture/source roots.
- `fixture_provenance`: reference to the wrapper below.
- `native_shell:{rendered_prefix:["/bin/bash","-lc"],executable:REF}`: exact
  observed native public-command rendering. The regular executable reference
  must reopen resolved `/usr/bin/bash`, matching `/bin/bash`; no alternate prefix,
  additional wrapper argument or unpinned executable is accepted.
- `protected_thread_ids`: at least three distinct nonempty exact native thread
  IDs, including the invoking process's `CODEX_THREAD_ID` and lead/author/reviewer
  conversations. The fixture exact thread must not be any of them. Session IDs
  remain grouping metadata; neither those nor daemon PID substitute thread IDs.

`schemas` contains exactly the sixteen generated v2 schema references for
`Thread{Read,GoalGet,TurnsList,ItemsList,QueueList,BackgroundTerminalsList,Start,
ShellCommand}{Params,Response}`. `NativeSchemaProvenance` binds the same schemas,
executable, output_root, generation_command and version_command references.
Literal generation argv is `EXE app-server generate-json-schema --experimental
--out ROOT`; version argv is `EXE --version` with observed `0.160.0`. These
retained command records reopen actual exits/stdout/stderr; they do not rerun
generation. The experimental flag is necessary for the queue/process schemas.
Optional absent `nextCursor` is normalized to terminal null only after reopening
its optional/nullable native schema; observations retain
`cursor_field_present:false`. Explicit non-null cursors are traversed completely.

## NativeStopFixture wrapper and literal proofs

The separately admitted lead fixture operator emits raw proofs; the lead can
assemble this wrapper without asserting stop acceptance:

```
{schema_version:1, kind:"NativeStopFixture", fixture_id,
 fixture_launch:REF, initial_goal:REF, payload_running:REF,
 operator:{candidate,materialization:REF,retention:REF,review:REF},
 workspace,output,common_git,command_sha256}
```

The operator review kind is `independent-native-fixture-source-review`, binding
exact candidate/parent/tree/source/materialization/retention, author/reviewer,
distinct nonempty `author_native_thread_id`/`reviewer_native_thread_id`, and
`operator_sha256` of `tests/collab/fixture_support/native_stop_fixture.py`.
Source is independently reconstructed from retained raw Git, not the mutable
author checkout. Operator author equals the admission's producer identity.

`fixture_launch` is the original `NativeFixtureLaunch` with creation, invocation,
operator_authorization, payload_output and actual_git_identity. The authorization
is `NativeFixtureLaunchAdmission` and pins the same source/review/runtime/tools,
workspace/base/branch, workspace/common Git device+inode and fixed command hash.
The observer reopens actual clean linked-worktree Git facts at its exact admitted
base; it must be separate from canonical, sharing the declared canonical `.git`.
Its actual NUL-delimited status is `git_facts.status_z_hex`, which must be empty;
an old literal `status:""` claim cannot substitute for this real readback.

Creation and invocation are literal `NativeFixtureRPC` records: kind/schema,
method, params, response, started_ms, ended_ms, transport_incarnation. Creation
is `thread/start` with never approval, danger-full-access, the exact three write
roots and fixed no-goal fixture instructions, with `environments` **omitted**. The
pinned native `ThreadStartParams.properties.environments` distinguishes omission
(default environment when access is enabled), an empty list (access disabled)
and a supplied nonempty list (first environment selected). This fixture permits
only exact default omission; `[]`, null or any supplied list refuses. The first
failed fixture with disabled environment access remains retained; this correction
does not retry its mutation, release its ownership or authorize cleanup. Its actual
returned thread must be fresh (`turns:[]`) with exact cwd. `initial_goal` is the
actual ordered `thread/goal/get` response `{goal:null}` between creation/launch.
Invocation is **one** `thread/shellCommand` with exact thread/command and
`timeoutMs:90000`; its immediate empty result does not imply termination or
invent a turn ID. The observer derives and freezes the sole actual fresh turn
from complete native paginated reads and binds its command item by command SHA.
The launch/wrapper `command_sha256` pins the submitted inner command. The native
public command is independently rendered as
`shlex.join(["/bin/bash","-lc",submitted_command])`; the tool item must match this
exact rendered digest. Bare equality, fuzzy matching, changed payloads, alternate
prefixes or trailing arguments refuse. Both literal commands, their distinct
digests and the shell executable reference are retained in the observer report's
`native_command_provenance`. A rendering match never substitutes for the real
payload/process/ancestry/terminal-tool proof. Both original unsuccessful preflight
attempts remain UNKNOWN and retained, without retry, release or cleanup authority.

The command is reconstructed independently with `shlex.join`: pinned systemd-run
`--user --scope --unit sureal-sustained-collab-ID --property MemoryMax=134217728
--property MemorySwapMax=0 --` pinned Python `-I -B` pinned operator `payload
--output OUTPUT/payload --fixture-id ID`.

`payload_running` is original `NativeFixturePayload`: fixture_id, source ref,
actual `{boot_id,pid,start_ticks,parent_pid,uid}` and actual scope
`{path,device,inode,memory_max:"134217728",memory_swap_max:"0"}`. Flags such as
`children_spawned` or `scientific_or_source_writes` are not accepted as oracles.
The reviewed payload lasts60s and the operator keeps its foreground connection
for95s. These fixed bounds accommodate measured source/cold verification startup
cost while retaining the observer120s limit; they permit no general timeout widening.
The observer independently reads actual payload argv/birth, scope members/caps
and native launch ancestry, stopping before the pinned shared daemon. Missing
parent/process coverage refuses; it never enrolls the daemon as an owned tool.
The native launch parent may lie outside the payload scope. A native null PID or
absent PTY handle is legitimate only with exact executed command item and this
corroborated command-written process/ancestry/scope evidence.

## Stop proof, privacy and disposition

First retain a nonempty in-progress native turn+single userShell command with
actual running payload/process witness. Empty history/schema/scan cannot pass.
Then retain two consistent observations at least5s apart: exact thread idle,
all actual turns terminal, all command items terminal with actual exit codes,
goal absent, complete submission queue empty, all native background handles
empty, original known process births gone, scoped membership empty and no
unexplained writer to workspace/output/common Git. Scan gaps refuse. If the
original scope disappears, retain its actual absence, not invented current
inode/caps. Unexpected turns/tools/history, active goal, incomplete pages,
changed source/runtime or missing facts remain explicit UNKNOWN.
Initial read records survive native validation, kernel coverage and retention
failures. A snapshot clears the bounded in-memory read buffer only after its
exact records are durably written; failures retain allowlisted responses in
`incomplete_native_observation` when the unchanged output budget permits.
This adds diagnostic evidence, never substitutes a missing running tool witness
or changes the mandatory stop proof. The original third failed probe remains
UNKNOWN and unchanged; its discarded historical reads are not reconstructed.

Only public allowlisted metadata is retained: IDs, statuses, cwd, process handles,
exit codes and command digest. Private reasoning/message/tool output, credentials,
unrelated notifications and unrelated session bodies are discarded. Kernel scans
retain only relevant scoped path/FD hits and coverage gaps, not unrelated data.

`report.json` kind `IndependentNativeStopPreflight` returns exit0 only for
`status:"pass",stop_capability:true`; exit3 is UNKNOWN. Every result explicitly
sets `task50_accepted:false` and `managed_dispatch_accepted:false`. Failures grant
neither ownership release nor cleanup. Retain all original witnesses, command
records and failures. Live proof and independent audit still follow source review.
